//
// Probe: the text and colour half of `bund/console` (D214).
//
// A golden strips ANSI, so what this pins is the text each word prints and
// that each prints one line: the colours and fades are pinned by the unit
// tests in `console_text.rs`, against the escapes `rusty-termcolor` 0.1.62
// writes. `console.text.randomcolor` is not here: its colour escape varies by
// run, and the debugger's stepping test compares a probe's raw bytes. What
// else this pins:
//
//   - **`console.text` converts**: a number prints as its text.
//   - **`console.box` pushes** its box, which `println` then prints; a
//     message of two lines is boxed as two rows, padded to the longer.
//   - **`console.title` and `console.clear`** print escapes only, and no
//     newline.
//
"probe: console.text and its colours print one line each" println
"plain" console.text
"red" console.text.red
"green" console.text.green
"blue" console.text.blue
"magenta" console.text.magenta
"cyan" console.text.cyan
"yellow" console.text.yellow

"probe: a number is converted" println
42 console.text
3.5 console.text.red

"probe: the fades print one line each" println
"all is well" console.text.ok
"careful" console.text.warning
"broken" console.text.error

"probe: console.box pushes the box" println
"boxed" console.box println
"Hello" "World!" " " swap + + console.box

"probe: console.title and console.clear print escapes only" println
"A title" console.title
console.clear
"after" println
